        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Peru votes for its ninth president in 10 years Americas Issued on: 07/06/2026 - 10:34 Peruvians will choose on Sunday their ninth president in 10 years, in a tight runoff election between conservative Keiko Fujimori and leftist Roberto Sanchez who are trying to woo voters fed up with political chaos and rising crime. Fujimori, daughter of former autocratic president Alberto Fujimori, is making her fourth bid for the presidency. 'Deplorable issues' cloud 2026 FIFA World Cup, deemed 'one of the least anticipated of this era' 04/06/2026 Sport 2026 World Cup: National teams begin to arrive in North America 04/06/2026 Sport US finds huge tunnel on the Mexican border used to smuggle drugs 03/06/2026 Americas Wembanyama chases NBA dream ahead of Spurs-Nicks final 03/06/2026 Americas As California votes in the primary elections, who are the candidates? 03/06/2026 Americas Californian elections test for divided Democrats on pivotal primary election day 03/06/2026 Americas Pro-Trump candidate lead in Colombia 'part of Donroe doctrine' asserting itself in region 01/06/2026 Americas Centenary of Marilyn Monroe: 'Just as relevant now as she was then' 01/06/2026 Culture How to handle armed groups? Colombians vote in presidential election 31/05/2026 Americas"
